.TH MYGREP 3 "2024" "libmyutils" "User Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search for lines containing a pattern in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep()
function searches through the file stream pointed to by
.IR fp
for lines containing the string
.IR search_str .
Matching lines are stored in a dynamically allocated array pointed to by
.IR matches .
The caller is responsible for freeing the allocated memory.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines found, or -1 on failure.
